{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2273","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2273","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2273\",\"parent_revision\":\"6b959e547ad320476afc0cd7659ed4681d52f59f706ae34bb1229eb1b49bd40c\",\"root_revision\":\"6b959e547ad320476afc0cd7659ed4681d52f59f706ae34bb1229eb1b49bd40c\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add local filesystem artifact fallback to backlog_core artifactbackend** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Investigation session: dh plugin path inconsistency analysis (2026-05-14)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-14\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:df565eb675311234fe272d95f0d32cf7 -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/` \u2014 primary changes\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/task_config.py` \u2014 search path addition only\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-14)\\n\\n### Concerns\\n\\n- [x] CONTRACT GAP: test_explicit_local_backend scenario missing from test_artifact_provider_fallback.py \u2014 spec \u00a78 line 851 requires a test that BACKLOG_BACKEND=local selects local provider directly without fallback attempt (reported by contract-verification on T08) \u2014 RESOLVED: test added and committed at 3268c76b\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nWhen no remote backend is configured (or the configured backend is unreachable), all MCP artifact tools \u2014 `artifact_register`, `artifact_read`, `artifact_list`, `artifact_get` \u2014 fail immediately. Agents receive `{\\\"error\\\": \\\"...\\\"}` and fall back to writing files at self-invented paths, producing inconsistent output locations across different agent files.\\n\\nThe root cause is that `_get_artifact_provider()` raises `GitHubUnavailableError` immediately when `DEFAULT_REPO` is unset, and `create_artifact_provider()` raises `BacklogError` for `sqlite` and `memory` enum entries \u2014 neither implements `ArtifactBackend`. No fallback chain exists.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Required Outcome\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. `artifact_register`, `artifact_read`, `artifact_list`, `artifact_get` succeed in all environments by transparently falling back to a `LocalFilesystemArtifactProvider` when the configured remote backend is unavailable.\\n2. The local provider stores its manifest index at `{project_root}/.dh/artifacts.json`.\\n3. Artifact content files remain at `{git_project_root}/{artifact_id}` (existing convention, unchanged).\\n4. The `.dh/` subdirectory is added to the backend TOML search path in `backlog_core/backend_protocol.py` and `sam_schema/core/task_config.py` so projects can commit `.dh/backend.toml` to select their backend.\\n5. A `sync_to_remote()` stub is included in the local provider, enabling future sync to a configured backend.\\n6. Agents calling MCP artifact tools never need to know or choose a file path.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"514397dd898a5bbb9e3c17079b1439ce0fb7db9cba69d518d6a0c87985c88eea\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCT3aA\"}"}